Extract `auditor_prelude()` + `run_turn_tools()` from `auditor_agent`'s
closure into module-level helpers exported from `inspect_petri._auditor`.

`auditor_prelude` is the ~45-line per-execute setup (model roles,
tape-wrapped `generate`/`today`, config-digest guard, template render,
compaction/approval resolve). `run_turn_tools` is the ~18-line per-turn
tool-call block (eager-resume inject/strip, `execute_tools`,
`end_conversation` check). `auditor_agent`'s own loop is unchanged in
behaviour — it now calls the two helpers.

The workbench's `workbench_auditor` layers step-gating and
divergent-serve emit on top of the standard turn; with this it can
import the two helpers instead of duplicating the block and reaching
into `_auditor.agent` privates.

Apply on `inspect_petri` `tape-replay-v2-l2-history`.

